17b608478ae845c43c637b"], "question": {"text": "A flask contains a mixture of isohexane and <math><mn>3</mn></math> -methylpentane. One of the liquids boils at <math><msup><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> while the other boils at <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> What is the best way to separate the two liquids and which one will be distilled out first?"}, "options": [{"id": "1dce69", "text": "fractional distillation, isohexane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d1"}, {"id": "47591c", "text": "simple distillation, <math><mn>3</mn></math> -methylpentane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d2"}, {"id": "9a9a46", "text": "simple distillation, isohexane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d3"}, {"id": "ed488c", "text": "fractional distillation, <math><mn>3</mn></math> -methylpentane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ef"], "concepts": ["6162fbaf6ed13040ec851d05"], "question": {"text": "Reagent, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthylamine and sulphanilic acid in acetic acid is used for the detection of"}, "options": [{"id": "04a079", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d6"}, {"id": "123ff7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92740d7"}, {"id": "966579", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>